// SHARPENED MINIMAL REPRO (corpus-bugfix, trunk a2157b996, 2026-07-21) — supersedes the older
// "2-hop / reachability" framing in mlrepro-cdz-check-false-cdz0201-const-provability-*.cdz (now RESOLVED-*).
//
// TWO updates vs the old finding:
//   1. The check-vs-compile DIVERGENCE is GONE: `cdz check` and `cdz compile` now AGREE on the corpus
//      program (both CDZ0201). So the "check rejects, compile accepts+runs=6" divergence no longer
//      reproduces on trunk — that half is fixed.
//   2. A RESIDUAL const-provability gap remains, and it is NOT about hop-count or reachability. The exact
//      minimal trigger is ANNOTATING `fold`'s intermediate `it` parameter as `it: Iter`.
//
// This is why corpus case 09-functions.sexp:316 ("a closed literal closure forwarded through const-wrapper
// hops is not a false reject", owned+pinned as todo by v-core-opt in 6525f56ab) is still graded `todo` on
// all 3 targets: actual = rejected [CDZ0201], expected = (output (: 6 Int64)).
//
// BISECT (const g stays const; only fold's it/acc annotations vary):
//   def fold(it,        acc,        g: ...) => OK, runs 6.
//   def fold(it,        acc: Int64, g: ...) => OK, runs 6.
//   def fold(it: Iter,  acc,        g: ...) => CDZ0201 REJECT.   <-- the single trigger
//   def fold(it: Iter,  acc: Int64, g: ...) => CDZ0201 REJECT (the corpus-case shape).
//
// So: annotating the Iter-typed intermediate param — the one whose `match it with Iter.Mk(s, step)`
// destructures the stored `step` closure out of the constructor — makes the SEPARATE const closure arg `g`
// lose its compile-time-known provability through the forward into drive's `const g`. Dropping the `it: Iter`
// annotation (inferring it) restores const-provability. LIKELY LOCUS: const-argument provability keys off a
// resolved/annotated binder shape for the Iter param and conflates the destructured-closure `step` path with
// the const `g` path. Routed to v-core-opt (owns this const-elaboration case + the todo pin).
//
// The minimal REJECTING program (drop `it: Iter` -> compiles + runs 6):
type Iter = | Mk(List(Int64), List(Int64) -> Option((Int64, List(Int64))))
def from-list(xs: List(Int64)) = Iter.Mk(xs, fn(s: List(Int64)) => match s with | [] => Option.None(unit) | [h, .. t] => Option.Some((h, t)))
def drive(const step: List(Int64) -> Option((Int64, List(Int64))), s: List(Int64), acc: Int64, const g: Int64 -> Int64 -> Int64) =
  match step(s) with | Option.None(_) => acc | Option.Some(p) => (match p with | (x, s2) => drive(step, s2, g(acc, x), g))
def fold(it: Iter, acc, g: Int64 -> Int64 -> Int64) = match it with | Iter.Mk(s, step) => drive(step, s, acc, g)
def sum(it) = fold(it, 0, fn(a, x) => a + x)
def main() = sum(from-list([1, 2, 3]))
export { main }
